  "aiSummary": "This bill appropriates funds to increase teacher salaries, support special education services, provide free breakfast and lunch to all public school students, establish a device refresh program for student computers, and freeze enrollment in the Opportunity Scholarship program (which provides vouchers for private school tuition) while reducing its future funding.",
  "aiProArguments": "Supporters argue this bill strengthens public schools by raising teacher pay to improve recruitment and retention, ensuring students with disabilities receive adequate services, eliminating food insecurity through free meals, and equipping students with updated technology for learning. They contend these investments support academic achievement and address critical needs in public education.",
  "aiConArguments": "Opponents argue the bill redirects significant funding away from the Opportunity Scholarship program, which they say limits school choice options for lower and middle-income families who want alternatives to public schools. They contend the public school investments, while substantial, may not address underlying efficiency concerns and that phasing out the scholarship program eliminates an educational option some families prefer.",
